From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Composition animations, property sets and batches (6048)

Windows.UI.Composition's compositor gave E_NOTIMPL for property sets,
easing functions, key frame and expression animations, scoped and commit
batches, and StartAnimation did nothing. Programs that animate their
visuals (fades, slides, colour changes) either failed or waited for a
batch's Completed that never came.

New animation.c: property sets (by name and type, ICompositionPropertySet2
booleans), every object's Properties, linear and cubic bezier easing,
scalar/vector2/3/4/colour/quaternion key frame animations (IKeyFrameAnimation:
delay, duration, iterations, stop behaviour, expression key frames of
this.StartingValue), expression animations (kept, not evaluated), and
scoped and commit batches. Started animations are copied and stepped on the
compositor's thread on a timer; they write the visual's, brush's, clip's or
property set's value ("Offset", "Offset.Y", "Color", ...) and ask for a
commit. A batch tells its Completed handlers once it has ended and its
animations finished. IKeyFrameAnimation, KeyFrameAnimation, its enums and
ICompositionPropertySet2 are declared in the IDL.
---
diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/Makefile.in b/dlls/dcomp/Makefile.in
index 3a28584..6a7367a 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/Makefile.in
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
 SOURCES = \
 	classes.idl \
+	animation.c \
 	composition.c \
 	objects.c \
 	device.c \
diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/animation.c b/dlls/dcomp/animation.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d3f3d60
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/animation.c
@@ -0,0 +1,2253 @@
